From: rive
Subject: [PATCH 0062] load aot code on windows on arm

WAMR could not compile AOT code for Windows on Arm, nor load it. wamrc
knew no arm64 COFF machine. It left arm64's calls to aot_func_internal#n
as relocations, which the loader cannot resolve, where it applies x64's
itself. And it dropped the .rdata holding arm64's jump tables, which are
offsets with no relocations, where x64's absolute entries have them. For
an msvc target it chose the medium code model, which arm64 lacks, so arm64
keeps the small one, whose adrp reaches the data the loader maps beside the
code.

The loader knew no arm64 COFF machine or relocation. COFF keeps every
addend in the instruction it relocates: an adrp's in bytes, not pages, and
a load or store's in units of its access size. Code reaches each constant
by an adrp and a load, two relocations, which now share one slot, where
each took the next and a pair could straddle a page. __chkstk, which LLVM
calls for frames past a page, joins the arm64 symbols. And every map the
loader makes goes below 4GB as on x64, which keeps the code within an
adrp's reach of its data and lets a function table address it.

